cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BLABAN: Bio-inspired Learning Algorithms for Benchmarking Agent Navigation"
message: "If you use this code or the accompanying report, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Abdelrahman
    given-names: Noureldin
repository-code: "https://github.com/NoureldinAbdelrahman/blaban-18"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - metaheuristics
  - multi-agent systems
  - cooperative robotics
  - optimization
  - simulated annealing
  - genetic algorithm
  - particle swarm optimization
abstract: >-
  BLABAN is a metaheuristic optimization toolkit for multi-agent cooperative
  systems, developed for the MCTR 1021 course project at the German University
  in Cairo. It implements Simulated Annealing, Genetic Algorithm, a swarm-based
  optimizer and a novel population-based metaheuristic on a shared problem
  formulation, with reproducible experiments and benchmarking.
